hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today I'm  going to answer a question from one of  our readers reach you who wrote in  asking about work-life balance so the  exact question is hi Evan you always  send quite interesting notes to read  that really inspire me so thank you for  that I want to ask one thing would you  please advise me on how an entrepreneur  can balance or cope with personal and  professional life it seems very hectic  to carry on with zeal and satisfaction  if you're happy at work there's  something tense waiting at the personal  front if you're happy with your personal  aspects attention to work please help  warm regards with you thanks to the  question especially as an entrepreneur  it's hard it's really hard to balance  your personal in your business life  because we're so emotionally attached to  our business right a lot of times the  business is an extension of of what we  do what I find really helpful is first  to have a separate space so you may not  be able to afford in the office you know  if you're starting up I like having an  office that I can go to so I have my  home and then I have my office and I  know when I'm at home I'm doing home  stuff and when I'm at the office I can  focus on my business if you're working  from home try to create a separate space  that is just for your office and you  know when you go there you're working  and that's you know you're going to be  focused on that and try to get  everything accomplished and not get too  distracted by your personal things I  find when entrepreneurs have a huge mix  you know you're you know working out of  your kitchen and there's you know kids  coming in and out it's it's just really  frustrating so you want to have a clear  separation the next thing I find that  also helps instead of just physical  separation is have a time separation so  I'll block off hours in my week for work  so I'm going to be in the office for you  know these days and this time and I know  what I'm working on and then just as  important i'll block off things for  personal and family time and I treat  those as important as any really  important business  meeting so i'll try not to book things  on certain days so like saturdays i  won't work i won't go to you know  conferences or trade shows or anything  else because I book that off for family  time you know there's a there's an  exception we'll talk about it and see if  it's really worth it or not but still  usually won't go and that's just a  personal decision but it helps make sure  you have time to do your personal things  as well as your business things it is  easy to get distracted I find at least  for myself if you're having family time  or personal time you come up with an  idea for business you know a lot of the  best ideas you get for your company is  when you're relaxed and your your plane  you know how many great ideas you get in  the shower because you're you're relaxed  right when you're tense and and stressed  out you probably can cope with a lot of  good ideas so if you're playing with  your kids or if you're just relaxing or  hanging out with friends you'll probably  get some great ideas for your business  and what I try to do then is just write  it down you know take some notes send an  email to myself and then move on and can  be able to continue on with with  whatever was doing for that day I try  not to get distracted you know with the  phone and answer an email that come in  you know I've set time so when I'll do  emails so just having clear boundaries  between your personal life and your  business life I find really helps I know  it can still be hard but try to remember  that you know when you're spending your  time with your family your friends  that's your time with your family and  friends and shut up everything else and  don't bring your work home with you and  when you do get a great idea yo don't  ignore it i don't want you to lose  awesome ideas to your company but send  yourself a quick email or take a note so  you can come back to it when you are  focused on your work that being said  it's still hard you're going to work  crazy hours as an entrepreneur  especially to launch it and you do want  to make sure that you still have some  time for your friends and family because  otherwise you're going to burn up and  it's very calling or entrepreneurs will  spend crazy hours at the beginning and  burn out and quit their company and  you'll have much more success by working  less hours but keeping at it  is something every day to grow a  business you'll be more successful and  you'll also be a lot happier so  hopefully that answers your question  thank you everybody for watching if you  liked the video please give it a thumbs  up below make you want to do more of  these for you and I love you have to  think if you want to comment about this  video or if you have a question about  your own business feel free to leave in  the comments section below I always read  those I love seeing them come in it  makes my makes my day when I see new  comments coming in the videos I know get  back to you as well so thank you and  we'll see you on the next episode  you
 

